       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.           TSWCLNUP.
       AUTHOR.               CA YODER.
       DATE-WRITTEN.         APRIL 1999.
      *INSTALLATION.         GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER CO.

      *D* REMARKS.
      *D*
      *D*   THIS PROGRAM WILL BE USED TO CLEAN UP THE STOREROOM
      *D*   WITHDRAWAL WORKSHEET MEMBERS IN SWDATAFL.
      *D*
      *D*   CHANGE FIELD FILES-TO-KEEP TO THE NUMBER OF FILES TO
      *D*   SAVE.
      *D*
      *C* CHANGES.
      *C*
      *C* 07/16/2002   CA YODER
      *C*    INCREASED FILES-TO-KEEP TO 600.  THIS WAS APPROXIMATELY
      *C*    A WEEK'S WORTH OF FILES FOR FREEPORT.
      *C*
      *C* 09/12/2003   BRUCE GEISER
      *C*    ALLOWED FOR LARGER GAPS (30) IN NUBMERING SEQUENCE.
      *C*

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.    I-O-FEEDBACK IS I-O-FEEDBACK-AREA.

      ******************************************************************
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
      ******************************************************************
       FILE-CONTROL.

           SELECT MWRKLIST-I
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0301
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                 ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

      ******************************************************************
       DATA DIVISION.
      ******************************************************************

       FILE SECTION.

       FD  MWRKLIST-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MWRKLIST-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0300  OF MCFLCS0301.

      ******************************************************************
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
      ******************************************************************
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  Q C M D E X C   F I E L D S
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  RMVM-CMD.
           05  PIC X(32)     VALUE "RMVM FILE(*LIBL/SWDATAFL) MBR(SW".
           05  RMVM-SEQ      PIC X(4).
           05  PIC X(1)      VALUE ")".

       01  RMVM-LEN          PIC S9(10)V9(5) COMP-3 VALUE 37.

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  M I S C E L L A N E O U S   F I E L D S
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  SEQ-NUMBER               PIC 9(4).
       01  SEQ-ALPHA  REDEFINES SEQ-NUMBER  PIC X(4).

       01  OLDEST-FILE-TO-KEEP      PIC 9(5).
       01  NEXT-FILE-TO-DLT         PIC 9(4).

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  A R G U M E N T   V A L U E S
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  WL-ARG.
           05  WRKL-NO-LIT               PIC XX    VALUE "SW".
           05  WRKL-NO-INC               PIC 9(4)  VALUE ZEROS.

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  F L A G S   A N D   S W I T C H E S
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  RTN-CODE                 PIC X.

       01  CLEANUP-COMPLETE         PIC X.

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  A C C U M U L A T O R S
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  FILE-COUNTER             PIC 9(5).

       01  MISSING-FILES            PIC 9(3).

       01  CURR-SEQ-NO              PIC 9(4).
       01  CURR-SEQ-NO-R REDEFINES CURR-SEQ-NO
                                    PIC X(4).

       01  FILES-TO-KEEP            PIC 9(4) VALUE 600.

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  D A T A B A S E   A N D   F I L E   B U F F E R S
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       COPY MWRKLIST   IN COPYLIB.

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  D A T A B A S E   S T A T U S   A R E A
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  FILE-STATUS.
           05  FILE-STATUS-1             PIC X.
           05  FILE-STATUS-2             PIC X.

       COPY DBCSACCT OF COPYLIB.

       COPY DATAB    OF COPYLIB.

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  U T I L I T Y   A R E A
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       COPY TBLOWUP OF COPYLIB.

       COPY VCOMAREA OF COPYLIB.

      ******************************************************************
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
      ******************************************************************

       00-CONTROL.

           PERFORM 10-HSK.

           PERFORM 60-DELETE-MBRS.

           PERFORM 20-EOJ.

           GOBACK.

       10-HSK.

           OPEN INPUT      MWRKLIST-I.

           MOVE 0                        TO  WRKL-NO-INC.

      *---- GET THE SEQUENCE NUMBER FOR THE LAST SW FILE.
           PERFORM 9999-READ-MWRKLIST-INFO-I.
           MOVE WRKLIST-DATE (3:4) TO CURR-SEQ-NO-R.

      *---- ADD 10,000 TO THE NUMBER SO THAT IF THE SEQUENCE NUMBERS
      *---- HAVE ROLLED OVER FROM 9999 TO 0000, THE CORRECT FILES WILL
      *---- BE REMOVED BY USING JUST THE LAST 4 DIGITS OF FIELD
      *---- OLDEST-FILE-TO-KEEP.
           COMPUTE OLDEST-FILE-TO-KEEP = CURR-SEQ-NO
                                       + 10000
                                       - FILES-TO-KEEP.
           DISPLAY "OLDEST-FILE-TO-KEEP:  " OLDEST-FILE-TO-KEEP.

           MOVE "N" TO CLEANUP-COMPLETE.

       20-EOJ.

           CLOSE           MWRKLIST-I.

       60-DELETE-MBRS.

           PERFORM VARYING FILE-COUNTER FROM 1 BY 1
              UNTIL CLEANUP-COMPLETE = "Y"

              SUBTRACT FILE-COUNTER FROM OLDEST-FILE-TO-KEEP
                 GIVING NEXT-FILE-TO-DLT

      *------- CHECK FOR MEMBER IN SWDATAFL WITH THIS SEQ NUM

              INITIALIZE RTN-CODE
              MOVE NEXT-FILE-TO-DLT TO SEQ-ALPHA
              CALL "SWCHKOBJ" USING   SEQ-ALPHA   RTN-CODE

      *------- ASSUME THAT IF THERE ARE 30 MISSING FILES IN A ROW
      *------- THEN THERE ARE NO MORE STOREROOM FILES TO DELETE.
      *------- HOWEVER, IF THERE ARE 29 OR LESS FILES NOT FOUND BEFORE
      *------- ANOTHER STOREROOM FILE IS FOUND, THEN RESET THE
      *------- COUNTER AND CONTINUE DELETING LOOP.

              IF RTN-CODE = "1"
                 ADD 1 TO MISSING-FILES
                 IF MISSING-FILES = 30
                    MOVE "Y" TO CLEANUP-COMPLETE
                 END-IF
              ELSE
                 INITIALIZE MISSING-FILES
                 MOVE NEXT-FILE-TO-DLT TO RMVM-SEQ
                 CALL "QCMDEXC" USING  RMVM-CMD  RMVM-LEN
              END-IF
           END-PERFORM.

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *9999 UTILITY SECTION.
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       9999-BLOWUP.
           MOVE "TSWCLNUP" TO BU-PGM-NAME.
           CALL "TBLOWUP" USING BASE, BU-PGM-NAME, STATUS-AREA,
              VIEW-COMAREA, FILE-STATUS, BU-DISPLAY-MSG,
              BU-DISPLAY-FLDS.

      *---------------------------------
      * MWRKLIST-INFO
      *---------------------------------

       9999-READ-MWRKLIST-INFO-I.
           MOVE 0 TO COND-WORD.
           MOVE WL-ARG TO WLKEY OF MWRKLIST-REC-I.
           READ MWRKLIST-I INTO BUF-MWRKLIST
               INVALID KEY MOVE FILE-STATUS TO FILE-STATUS.
           IF FILE-STATUS NOT = "00"
              MOVE "READ MWRKLIST-INFO*9999-RMI" TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG
              MOVE WL-ARG TO BU-DISPLAY-FLD (1)
              GO TO 9999-BLOWUP.

